# Line endings are not a style preference here: hooks/subagent-dispatch-log.sh is executed
# by `sh`, and benchmark/scenarios/*.sh by `bash`. A CR in a shebang or at the end of a
# command breaks both. Two of this repo's CI checks also assert that those files are
# LF-only — with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a fresh clone would check them
# out as CRLF and those checks would fail on a contributor's machine but pass on the Linux
# runner. A gate whose result depends on the operating system is not a gate.

* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
